nack food and beverage products in Latin America, North America, Asia, the Middle East, Africa, and Europe. The company provides biscuits and baked snacks, including cookies, crackers, salted snacks, snack bars, and cakes and pastries; chocolates; and gums and candies, as well as various cheese, grocery, and powdered beverage products. Its brand portfolio includes Oreo, Ritz, LU, CLIF Bar, Tate's Bake Shop biscuits and baked snacks, Cadbury Dairy Milk, Milka, and Toblerone chocolate. It serves supermarket chains, wholesalers, supercenters, club stores, mass merchandisers, distributors, convenience stores, gasoline stations, drug stores, value stores, and other retail food outlets through direct store delivery, company-owned and satellite warehouses, distribution centers, third-party distributors, and other facilities, as well as through independent sales offices and agents. The company also sells products directly to businesses and consumers through e-retail platforms, retailer digital platforms, as well as through its direct-to-consumer websites and social media platforms. Mondelez International, Inc. was formerly known as Kraft Foods Inc. and changed its name to Mondelez International, Inc. in October 2012. The company was incorporated in 2000 and is headquartered in Chicago, Illinois.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Dirk  Van de Put | Chairman & CEO | Age 65 | Compensation: $5.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 91K people. Revenue per employee of $423K ranks in the below the sector median among Consumer Defensive peers. Each employee generates $36K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $1K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 13\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Mondelez International, Inc. is a large-cap consumer defensive business with a $83.9B market cap on $38.5B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +7% over the past three years and +3% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 7% against a 6% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically, with gross margins sitting at 38%.","The business throws off $3.2B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 8 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.84\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 4.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and interest coverage runs at 5.9\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 5.8% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Carries a 45% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.45256797583081565},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $26.1M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Consumer Defensive peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Consumer Defensive peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"High market volatility with VIX at 36, signaling elevated fear","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"GLP-1 and health-trend demand destruction \u2014 weight-loss drugs and wellness shifts are structurally reducing consumption in snack, beverage, and packaged food categories.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["24 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Consumer Defensive sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 15% over 3 months","Consumer Defensive ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Consumer Defensive tends to hold up well as investors rotate into defensive names"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Can Higher Spending Drive Global Growth at Mondelez (NASDAQ:MDLZ)?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/consumer/can-higher-spending-drive-global-growth-at-mondelez-nasdaqmdlz","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795152540.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.758,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Is Mondelez (NASDAQ:MDLZ) Increasing Its Global Brand Support?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/consumer/is-mondelez-nasdaqmdlz-increasing-its-global-brand-support","date":"2026-11-19","timestamp":1795063200.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.599,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Melania Trump reveals husband Donald's favorite cookies - but she hates them","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/melania-trump-reveals-husband-donalds-212700000.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795210933.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.606,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"19 logos you probably didn't know had hidden meanings","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/19-logos-probably-didnt-know-182502000.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":17952